WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.506
Week 12: Shopping, Clothing, and Demonstratives. ask for an item and size compare price and fit return or exchange a purchase

2
00:00:08.506 --> 00:00:16.287
Cultural lens. Fixed prices, bargaining contexts, sizes, taxes, receipts, and consumer expectations.

3
00:00:16.287 --> 00:00:28.145
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:28.145 --> 00:00:39.768
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:39.768 --> 00:00:48.597
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:48.597 --> 00:01:18.375
Model language. Algunas tiendas tienen precio fijo. — Some stores have fixed prices. En otros lugares se puede regatear. — In other places you can bargain. El impuesto se suma al precio final. — The tax is added to the final price. La talla local no siempre coincide con la internacional. — The local size doesn't always match the international one. El consumidor espera un trato justo. — The consumer expects fair treatment.

7
00:01:18.375 --> 00:01:28.123
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
